cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AdaptiGuard: An Empirical Case Study of Measurement Validity in the Evaluation of LLM-Agent Defenses"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. Do not cite it as a confirmed, state-of-the-art, or production defense."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shirazi Matin
    given-names: Seyed Mohammadreza
    email: mrshirazimatin@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  AdaptiGuard is an empirical case study showing how measurement decisions in
  the evaluation of LLM-agent defenses can change conclusions on the same
  underlying traces. It examines candidate measurement validity checks for
  runtime-defense evaluation: the success endpoint, blocked-payload labeling,
  scenario validity, authorship independence, per-model reporting against a
  noise floor, and defense-channel verification. It is not a defense, a
  production security tool, or a general benchmark. Manuscript package:
  docs/paper/negative_result/.
keywords:
  - LLM security
  - prompt injection
  - evaluation validity
  - measurement validity
  - negative result
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/MohammadRezaShiraziMatin/adapti-guard"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-14"
